cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use apairo in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "apairo: a unified loader for robotics sensor datasets"
abstract: >-
  apairo gives synchronous and asynchronous robotics sensor datasets one Python
  API. Each channel is described by three declarative contracts -- how its
  frames are ordered, how one frame is decoded, and what each frame's alignment
  key is -- so a dataset is read where it lies instead of being rewritten.
  Filtering, channel selection, joining and resampling onto a reference clock
  are lazy views that cost index arrays rather than copies, and every temporal
  match reports which event backs it and how stale that event is.
type: software
